     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, a lower starting dose of 500 mg PO two or three times daily with meals.\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
